# L0: status of the four-card set, an all-four reset with the heal (so every run after it starts from freshly trained boards, and a
# card, link or hugepage fault fails here, before an hour of engine builds), then build the tp4-lanes image. Run first: it is the
# cheapest job and the only one every later job depends on. It runs the image copy-closure and overlay tests inside the P8 base
# first, then G1 provenance, and tags the image only if they pass, so a closure error fails here with no card touched.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card lanes window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it
# over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lanes and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image L0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock): status 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 min (up to 12); build 7-15 min when the image's layers are cached
# (the bundle stage is; only the overlay and the profiles are new), 30-70 min cold (step limit 75).
# Read: the status listing (four boards by id, one firmware bundle on all of them, at least four free 1 GiB hugepages, no holders, NO
# platform serving container, disk for a new ~32 GB image), then the build log (closure tests OK, provenance passed).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lanes-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
